Take cpuinfo from the system instead of the network.  Upstream 1.31.0 dropped
the "FIND_PACKAGE_ARGS NAMES cpuinfo" its Linux FetchContent declare carried
in 1.29.0, so with FETCHCONTENT_FULLY_DISCONNECTED=ON configure falls back to
a download that cannot work on OBS and the cpuinfo::cpuinfo target is never
defined.  Restoring the find lets the system cpuinfo-devel be used, as in
1.29.0: it already ships cpuinfo_deinitialize (as a stub, exactly what 1.29.0
linked against), so behavior is unchanged.

diff --git a/cmake/external/onnxruntime_external_deps.cmake b/cmake/external/onnxruntime_external_deps.cmake
--- a/cmake/external/onnxruntime_external_deps.cmake
+++ b/cmake/external/onnxruntime_external_deps.cmake
@@ -396,6 +396,7 @@
           # https://github.com/pytorch/cpuinfo/pull/400
           ${Patch_EXECUTABLE} --binary --ignore-whitespace -p1 <
           ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/patches/cpuinfo/enable_deinit_refcounting.patch
+      FIND_PACKAGE_ARGS NAMES cpuinfo
       )
     else()
       onnxruntime_fetchcontent_declare(
